#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Guarded Nexus entrypoint for resuming tracked DSH goals.

This command does not own Issue completion, DSH goal lifecycle, provider routing,
leases, verification, merge, or release. It stores a durable tracking binding
for a DSH session and re-reads authoritative workflow state before any resume
can launch the DSH process. Any BLOCK_RESUME decision exits 75; the provider is
never invoked unless the decision is ALLOW_RESUME.

The ``red-gate`` subcommand is a deterministic, outer, pre-mutation test-evidence
gate. It does not trust a model's RED_READY claim: from a controller-written
contract it inspects the worktree diff (test-only changes, no duplicate
definitions, no oracle asserting the buggy literal), re-runs the target pytest
nodes with an explicit interpreter, and requires every node to fail with the
contracted assertion signature. Any REVISE_RED decision exits 75. It holds no
verifier or completion authority.
"""

